            <ArticleTitle>Improvement of the activity and thermostability of microbial transglutaminase by multiple-site mutagenesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/09168451.2017.1403881</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Microbial transglutaminase (MTG) is an enzyme widely used in the food industry. Mutiple-site mutagenesis of Streptomyces mobaraensis transglutaminase was performed in Escherichia coli. According to enzymatic assay and thermostability study, among three penta-site MTG mutants (DM01-03), DM01 exhibited the highest enzymatic activity of 55.7 ± 1.4 U/mg and longest half-life at 50 °C (418.2 min) and 60 °C (24.8 min).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
